  "nl_text": "The rschema_0095 database is designed to manage customer interactions and employee activities within a company. The Customer table stores information about each customer, including their address, company name, email, gender, name, phone number, and a unique customer ID. The Employee table contains details about each employee, such as their department, email, gender, level, name, phone number, and position. The Sales_Opportunity table tracks sales opportunities, including the actual transaction period, creation time, estimated amount, estimated transaction date, opportunity name, stage, and status. It links customers and employees through their IDs, and the primary key is a composite of the customer ID, employee ID, and creation time. The Communication_Record table records communication between customers and employees, including the communication content, method, result, stage, and creation time, with a composite primary key of customer ID, employee ID, and creation time. The Service_Request table logs service requests from customers, including the creation time, request description, type, solution, and status, linked to customers and employees through their IDs, with a composite primary key of customer ID, employee ID, and creation time.",
  "gold_question": "Customer Relationship Management (CRM) systems are tools used by companies to manage interactions with customers, improve customer satisfaction and loyalty, and optimize sales and marketing processes. With increasing competition and changes in the market environment, many companies have realized that maintaining and improving relationships with customers is essential for long-term success. Through efficient customer data management, accurate market segmentation, timely customer follow-up, and personalized services, companies can increase customer stickiness, improve sales and service quality, and thus achieve higher market share and customer satisfaction.\nCRM systems help companies manage customers comprehensively by integrating basic customer information, communication records, sales opportunities, service requests, etc. This system not only improves the work efficiency of marketing and sales teams, but also helps customer service departments provide more personalized services, thereby forming healthy customer relationships.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0095.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0095\nCREATE TABLE `customer` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) NOT NULL,\n  `company_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `employee` (\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) NOT NULL,\n  `department` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `level` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `position` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `sales_opportunity` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `opportunity_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `estimated_transaction_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `estimated_amount` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stage` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`, `employee_id`, `creation_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `sales_opportunity_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `sales_opportunity_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`employee_id`) REFERENCES `employee` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `communication_record` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `communication_content` text NOT NULL,\n  `method` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `result` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stage` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`, `employee_id`, `creation_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `communication_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `communication_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`employee_id`) REFERENCES `employee` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `service_request` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `request_description` text NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `solution` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`, `employee_id`, `creation_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `service_request_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `service_request_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`employee_id`) REFERENCES `employee` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
